WEBVTT

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:01.976
and not the end itself.

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:07.976
I believe it was one great
philosopher who said --

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:09.938
no, no -- Cervantes.

00:13:09.962 --> 00:13:15.214
Cervantes said, "The journey
is better than the end."

00:13:15.238 --> 00:13:17.047
And I like that.

00:13:17.071 --> 00:13:19.302
I think that it is --
it's getting there.

00:13:19.326 --> 00:13:22.017
Sometimes when you get there,
there's almost a let down.

00:13:22.041 --> 00:13:24.065
But it's the getting there that's the fun.

00:13:24.089 --> 00:13:28.843
As a basketball coach at UCLA,
I liked our practices to be the journey,

00:13:28.867 --> 00:13:32.157
and the game would be
the end, the end result.